## Definition of a card -- in the outline style:  a heading, then what's true of it
a "card" is a thing where:

	## suit and rank
	- suit is a suit of its deck
	- its "color" is the color of its suit
	- its "rank" is a rank of its deck

	- it "is a (suit)"                      // e.g. "the card is a spade"
	- it "is a (rank)"                      // e.g. "the card is a queen"
	- it "is the (rank) of (suits)"         // e.g. "the card is the queen of spades"
	- it "is a face card" if its rank is a face card
	// CLAUDE TODO: doesn't work, should be `get isANumberCard`
	- it "is a number card" if it is not a face card
	- it "is a wild card" if it is not a joker

	## direction
	// CLAUDE TODO: `DIRECTIONS` should only be defined as Card.Directions
	- its direction is up or down
	- it "is face up" if its direction is up
	- it "is face down" if its direction is down

	## value and names
	- value is the position of its rank
	- its "name" is:
		if it is a joker return "joker"
		return its rank + "-of-" + its suit

	- its "short suit" is:
		// uncodoe: see https://www.compart.com/en/unicode/block/U+1F0A0
		if it is a club return "♣️"
		if it is a diamond return "♦️"
		if it is a heart return "♥️"
		if it is a spade return "♠️"
		return "?"
	- its "short rank" is:
		if it is a joker return "🃏"
		if its rank is a number return "" + its rank
		return the first character of its rank as uppercase
	- its "short direction" is:
		if its direction is up return "↑"
		return "↓"
	- its "state" is: its short rank + its short suit + its short direction

	## drawing
	- to "draw its front":
		<ui-button compact onClick={fire event card click with card = it} className="Card face-up [rank] [suit]" color={its color} compact fluid>
			{its short rank + " "}
			<span className="suit">{its short suit}</span>
		</ui-button>
	- to "draw its back":
		<ui-button compact onClick={fire event card click with card = it} className="Card face-down [rank] [suit]" compact fluid>
			<ui-icon name="bicycle" fitted/>
		</ui-button>

	## actions -- the sentence style, beside the outline

	// Turn card face up or face down
	// Note that this will animate if you `wait for turn the card face up`
	- to turn it face up:
		set its direction to up
		pause for 50 msec
	to turn it face down:
		set its direction to down
		pause for 50 msec

	// Flip card to opposite direction
	// Note that this will animate if you `wait for turn the card face up`
	to turn it over:
		if its direction is up: turn it face down
		otherwise: turn it face up
		pause for 50 msec

a joker is a card
	- its rank is "joker"
	- its suit is its color
	- its color is red or black
	- its "short suit" is "🃟"
	- its value is 53 if it is black otherwise 54


## create a card instance with default properties
to test card setup
	get a new card whose rank is queen, suit is spades and direction is up
	its rank should be queen
	its suit should be spades
	its name should be "queen-of-spades"
	its color should be black
	its value should be 12
	its short suit should be "♠️"
	its short rank should be "Q"

	it is face up should be yes
	it is face down should be no

	it is a face card should be yes
	it is not a face card should be no
	it is a joker should be no
	it is a wild card should be no

	it is a spade should be yes
	it is a club should be no

	it is a queen should be yes
	it is a joker should be no
	it is an ace should be no
	it is a 2 should be no

	it is the queen of spades should be yes
	it is the queen of clubs should be no
	it is not the 2 of diamonds should be yes

	turn it face down
	its direction should be down

	turn it over
	it is face up should be yes

	// test jokers
	joker is a new joker with color = red
	joker is a joker should be yes
	joker is a wild card should be yes
	joker is a face card should be yes
